    <h2>Service Areas Around Huntsville</h2>

    <p>If you're a Huntsville-based contractor, you probably serve more than just inside the city limits. Your website should reflect that. Beyond Huntsville proper, the typical service area includes <a href="/locations/madison/">Madison</a> (just west), <a href="/locations/athens/">Athens</a> (up I-65), <a href="/locations/decatur/">Decatur</a> (across the river), Hartselle, Meridianville, Hazel Green, Owens Cross Roads, and Gurley. We build pages for each of the cities you actually serve, so when someone in Owens Cross Roads searches for "plumber near me," your website has a fighting chance to show up.</p>

    <p>If your service area extends further — into the Shoals or down toward Cullman — we can build for those too. The "Large Site" build (up to 20 pages) is built specifically for contractors whose service area spans multiple distinct markets.</p>

    <h2>What Makes a Huntsville Contractor Website Actually Work</h2>

    <p>A few things matter more for Huntsville-area contractors than for contractors in other markets:</p>

    <p><strong>Mobile speed.</strong> Huntsville's homeowner demographic skews younger than other Alabama cities (the aerospace and tech economy attracts people in their 30s and 40s). That demographic does almost all of their contractor searching on phones. A website that takes more than 3 seconds to load on mobile loses 40% of its visitors before they ever see what you do.</p>

    <p><strong>Real photos.</strong> Stock photos kill conversion rates in Huntsville faster than in most markets. Tech-adjacent customers are sophisticated about marketing — they can spot a stock photo from a mile away, and they immediately distrust the business behind it. Photos of your actual truck, your actual tools, your actual finished work matter.</p>

    <p><strong>Specific service-area language.</strong> A homeowner in Hampton Cove searching for a plumber wants to know you'll actually come out to Hampton Cove. "Serving Huntsville and surrounding areas" is too vague. "We serve Hampton Cove, Big Cove, Monte Sano, Jones Valley, and central Huntsville daily" is specific enough to build trust.</p>

    <p><strong>Financing visibility.</strong> Huntsville's higher-income demographic still uses financing for major work — water heater replacements, HVAC system installs, roof replacements. If your website doesn't address financing options explicitly, you're losing a chunk of qualified buyers who can't write a $9,000 check at the moment of decision.</p>

    <h2>How We're Different From a Marketing Agency</h2>

    <p>We're not a marketing agency. Marketing agencies sell complicated multi-channel packages at $2,500-$5,000/month, mostly to contractors who don't need that scale of investment yet. We build the foundation: a real website that exists, a Google Business Profile that's fully filled out, and a steady drip of content that grows your search visibility over time. That's it. No "social media management" you don't need. No "PPC campaign optimization" billed at $1,200/month. Just the fundamentals, done right.</p>

    <p>If you're a Huntsville contractor doing $3M+ a year, a full marketing agency might genuinely be a good fit for you. If you're doing under $3M, you almost certainly don't need that level of complexity. You need the basics, executed well. That's what we do.</p>

